# Stalwart Successor triggers for "a creature you control" (CR 603.2), entering with counters included (CR 122.6) and not just
# itself: Bot1's Walking Ballista enters with one counter and gets another from it. Bot2's Walking Ballista, entering with a counter
# on turn 2, is not Bot1's creature: it keeps one counter and Bot1's Successor stays without any.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Lotus Petal
Walking Ballista
Stalwart Successor
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Walking Ballista
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stalwart Successor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot2.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Stalwart Successor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Stalwart Successor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
